<p>
  This Refund Policy explains how refunds work for website design, development and SEO
  services provided by ONYX, operated by
  <span class="legal__ph">[your registered business / proprietor name]</span>.
  It should be read alongside your project agreement and our
  <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
</p>

<h2>1. Deposits</h2>
<p>Projects usually begin with a deposit that reserves your slot and covers initial discovery
  and design work. Because that work starts immediately, the deposit is
  <strong>non-refundable</strong> once work has begun, unless we haven’t started.</p>

<h2>2. The “first concept” promise</h2>
<p>If, after we present the <strong>first design concept</strong>, you feel it isn’t the right
  fit, you may end the project there. In that case you keep what’s been delivered and owe only
  for work completed up to that point — <span class="legal__ph">[state whether the deposit is
  retained or partly refunded]</span>.</p>

<h2>3. Work in progress &amp; milestones</h2>
<p>For milestone-based projects, payments already made for <strong>completed and delivered</strong>
  milestones are non-refundable. Any amount paid in advance for work not yet started will be
  refunded if you cancel.</p>

<h2>4. SEO / ongoing services</h2>
<p>SEO and retainer services are delivered over time and depend on third-party search engines.
  Fees for a period already worked are non-refundable. You may cancel future periods with
  <span class="legal__ph">[e.g. 15 days’]</span> notice; you won’t be charged for periods after
  the notice takes effect.</p>

<h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a> with your project details and
  reason. We’ll review and respond within <span class="legal__ph">[7]</span> business days, and
  process any approved refund to your original payment method within
  <span class="legal__ph">[10]</span> business days.</p>

<h2>6. Chargebacks</h2>
<p>Please contact us first — we’d always rather resolve it directly than through a chargeback.</p>
